  "application_type_full": "Full planning & listed building consent",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The works to which this consent relates, must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this consent.\r\nReason: To accord with the provisions of Section 18(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation areas) Act 1990\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans, documents and specifications: \r\nDrawings 1203-WWA-B1-00-DR-A-0120(Rev.P06), 0121(Rev.P04) and 0122(Rev.P04), received 19/10/2026. Drawings 1203-WWA-00-EX-DR-A-0000(Rev.P04), 0021(Rev.P05), 0210(Rev.P03) and 0211(Rev.P03), and Heritage Assessment (dated April 2026), London Plan Fire Statement (V0.1, dated May 2026), Planning Design Access Statement (Rev.P02, dated August 2026), Planning Statement (1203_TA/AC, dated May 2026) and Report on the Condition of the Existing Building (04452, Rev.2, dated April 2026), received 13/10/2026.\r\nReason:  To ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - This consent does not permit the demolition or dismantling of any part of the listed building, or the removal of any internal/ external feature, floor, wall or ceiling surface, except in so far as the alterations hereby approved necessitate the removal of certain parts of the existing structure as specifically shown on the approved drawings.\r\nReason: To protect and preserve the character of the listed building.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - No development above ground level shall take place until full details and samples of all materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Details must include a detailed schedule of materials, a photographic sample board and rendered drawings, elevations and sections at a sufficient scale (1:20 or 1:50) to illustrate how all external materials will appear together. The submitted information should cover the following elements:\r\n(a)\tBrick/stonework (including brick, stone, masonry, brick panels, feature brick panel, brick framing feature and mortar on-site sample panel, minimum one metre by one metre) including all mortar colours, joint type, brick bond;\r\n(b)\tAny cladding materials / render (including specifications);\r\n(c)\tTiles / roof covering; including parapet coping / capping materials, dormers and canopies;\r\n(d)\tWindow types; and sectional drawings of reveals / courses / sills / textures / head details \r\n(e)\tBalustrading treatment for proposed ramped access (including details / sections / materials); \r\n(f)\tAny boundary treatment that may be required; and \r\n(g)\tAny other materials/details / fittings to be used (including solar panels, heat pumps, extract vents, rainwater goods, boiler flues etc.), with sections and on-site samples where appropriate.\r\nThe development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved details and maintained as such thereafter.\r\nReason: In order to protect the setting of the listed building and the appearance of the conservation area.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The existing historic mouldings (plaster pilasters and high-level capitals) and upper flight of the first to second floor historic staircase within proposed Flat 9 shall be retained and refurbished in line with the approved submissions, and the lower flight (including handrail) shall be carefully preserved and boxed in, as specified in the submitted Heritage Assessment.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the special architectural and historic interest of the listed building.\r\n",
    "Condition : 6 - No external utility boxes (for gas and electricity) shall be affixed to the building and any cables, wires, aerials, pipework, meter boxes or flues shall be discreetly integrated into the building and shall not be fixed to any elevation or roof slope facing a highway. \r\nNo fans, louvres, ducts, water tanks or other external plant shall be installed on the building hereby permitted without the prior written approval of the local planning authority. \r\nNo advertisements shall be displayed on the development without details of the advertisements having first been submitted to and approved in writing by the Council through securing of Advertisement Consent and/or Planning Permission. \r\nReason: In order to safeguard the visual amenity of the area and neighbours living conditions.\r\n"
  ],
